<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:sys="using:System"
             xmlns:dash="using:GalactiLog.App.ViewModels.Dashboard"
             xmlns:detail="using:GalactiLog.App.ViewModels.TargetDetail"
             xmlns:controls="using:GalactiLog.App.Controls"
             xmlns:t="using:GalactiLog.App.Controls.Table"
             x:Class="GalactiLog.App.Views.TargetDetail.FrameTableView"
             x:Name="Root"
             x:DataType="detail:FrameTableViewModel">
  <!-- design-spec 12.4's frame table, hosted on the session pane's one starred row since P12 R10
       retired the session accordion card (phase review P3-7). A header row and a ListBox rather
       than a DataGrid, for the reason ruling Q7 gave the dashboard:
       no DataGrid package is pinned, and dynamic column visibility plus a per-row expander plus a
       per-row action menu are more work to bend a DataGrid into than to lay out directly.

       32 explicit header cells and 32 explicit row cells is a long file, and it is the correct
       trade: compiled bindings check all 64 paths at build time. The alternative, a string-keyed
       cell lookup, checks none of them and turns a typo into a blank column at runtime.

       A header cell's IsVisible sits on its ContentControl, not on the button inside it (Phase 5
       review item 2): on the button, a hidden column leaves the container's width behind as a gap
       and every column to its right sits one cell out of line with the rows. Header and row cells
       bind one width per column (P24 R5), so the two collapse and resize in step.

       Cells bind ColumnViewModel.IsShown, which is the persisted visible list AND the
       metric-group gate (spec 5.8.2: the group toggle wins). The picker binds IsVisible, the
       persisted list, and disables a gated column rather than hiding it, so the user can see that
       the column exists and why it is not rendering.

       Nothing here sets FontSize. Scales.axaml's FontSize* keys are ratios, not point sizes, and
       FontSizeTokenTest fails the build on binding one to FontSize. Every colour is a theme token:
       the frame table renders no user-data colour, so there is no legitimate literal in this file.

       The header band and the rows pan together, because 32 columns will not fit: the ListBox
       scrolls both ways itself and the code-behind keeps the two horizontal offsets equal.

       The rows no longer carry a MaxHeight of their own (P12 Task 6). FrameRowsViewportHeight was
       a fixed 420 px bound that existed only because the table's host, the session accordion card,
       sat inside the detail page's vertical ScrollViewer and measured the rows against infinite
       height, so every row realised: the verification agent measured a 605 ms median UI-thread
       stall expanding a 200 frame session that way (FIXER LIST F12). The host is Task 5's session
       pane now and it gives the table a starred grid row, so the pane's own height is the viewport
       and VirtualizingStackPanel has something finite to virtualise against without this file
       guessing a number. Do not re-add a MaxHeight here: the bound belongs to whatever hosts the
       table, and FrameTableView_HasNoFixedViewportHeight is what fails if it comes back.

       The toolbar sits above that ScrollViewer rather than inside it, so the shown count and the
       three buttons stay put while the columns pan. The column picker moved into it for the same
       reason: at the end of the header row it sat at the far right of a 2600 px band. -->
  <UserControl.Resources>
    <!-- P24 R5: every keyed column's width is its ColumnViewModel.Width, which the header cell
         and the row cell both bind, so the two can never disagree. The view-model seeds it, the
         code-behind measures the auto-fit, and the divider at the right edge of each header cell
         drags it. The one fixed width left is the Rig column's, which has no key to store under. -->
    <sys:Double x:Key="FrameColTextWidth">90</sys:Double>

    <!-- R23: a watch or reject row is tinted in its band colour at an alpha every ink stays
         readable over in both themes (reject is the guide graph's failed-settle alpha); hover is
         one step stronger. The Colors are read live so a theme switch retints the rows. -->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FrameTintWatch" Color="{DynamicResource ColorWarningValue}" Opacity="0.12" />
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FrameTintWatchHover" Color="{DynamicResource ColorWarningValue}" Opacity="0.2" />
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FrameTintReject" Color="{DynamicResource ColorErrorValue}" Opacity="0.15" />
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="FrameTintRejectHover" Color="{DynamicResource ColorErrorValue}" Opacity="0.24" />

    <!-- One header cell: a button that sorts, showing the direction glyph on the active key. Every
         one of the 32 columns is sortable (spec 12.4), so unlike the dashboard's header there is
         no column here whose button the command ignores.

         The alignment is a class on the button rather than 32 attributes on the 32 header cells:
         the template's DataType is ColumnViewModel, so Classes.numeric binds IsNumeric directly
         and Theme/Controls.axaml's Button.header-cell(.numeric) setters do the rest. The chrome
         comes from the spine's Button.tc-head, the gutter is the button's Padding (the cell is a
         fixed Width, so a Margin would only narrow the hit area), and the title is the shared
         t-label header tier with the column's tip.

         The title sits in the Grid's star column (fixer-list item 20, phase 14C) so it measures
         against the cell's real width and TextTrimming can run; a StackPanel would offer it
         infinite width. The sort glyph is drawn on the side away from the alignment edge: before a
         numeric title and after a text one, so a title's aligned edge is its column's edge whether
         or not the column is the sort key (audit inconsistency 10, the dashboard's placement). -->
    <DataTemplate x:Key="FrameHeaderCell" DataType="dash:ColumnViewModel">
      <Grid>
        <Button Classes="header-cell tc-head"
                Classes.numeric="{Binding IsNumeric}"
                HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).SortByCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{Binding Key}"
                Padding="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.CellPadding}">
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto">
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="0"
                       Classes="t-label tc-sortglyph"
                       Text="{Binding SortGlyph}"
                       Margin="0,0,4,0"
                       IsVisible="{Binding IsNumeric}" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="1"
                       Classes="header-title t-label" Classes.numeric="{Binding IsNumeric}"
                       Text="{Binding Title}"
                       ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Tip}"
                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
            <TextBlock Grid.Column="2"
                       Classes="t-label tc-sortglyph"
                       Text="{Binding SortGlyph}"
                       Margin="4,0,0,0"
                       IsVisible="{Binding !IsNumeric}" />
          </Grid>
        </Button>
        <!-- P24 R5's divider, over the button's right edge, which is the cell's right gutter: a
             drag sets the column's width live and stores it on release; a double-click clears the
             stored width and refits. The code-behind owns the gesture, the way the lanes handle
             owns its own. -->
        <Border Classes="column-divider"
                Width="8"
                HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                Background="Transparent"
                Cursor="SizeWestEast"
                PointerPressed="OnDividerPressed"
                PointerMoved="OnDividerMoved"
                PointerReleased="OnDividerReleased"
                PointerCaptureLost="OnDividerCaptureLost">
          <Border Width="1"
                  Margin="0,4"
                  HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                  Background="{DynamicResource ColorBorderDefault}" />
        </Border>
      </Grid>
    </DataTemplate>
  </UserControl.Resources>

  <UserControl.Styles>
    <!-- A text header cell reads from its left edge; a numeric one reads over its figures
         (spec 14.4). Before this, the template hardcoded Left for all 32 while the rows
         right-aligned 26 of them, so a header sat at the far end of its own column
         (panel-density.md section 2, item 5). The two alignment setters are
         Theme/Controls.axaml's Button.header-cell and Button.header-cell.numeric: they carry no
         chrome, but a Button style declared in a view is what ControlStyleScanTest's choke-point
         rule fails on, and an exemption nobody has to remember is worth two lines in the shared
         vocabulary (P12 Task 5).

         One definition each for the two cell roles (spec 14.4's role rules). -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.header-title.numeric">
      <Setter Property="TextAlignment" Value="Right" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell">
      <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorTextSecondary}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Text may trim; a figure never does, so number cells fall through to Theme/Table.axaml's
         TextBlock.tc-num TextTrimming None (spec.md item 3). -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.tc-text">
      <Setter Property="TextTrimming" Value="CharacterEllipsis" />
    </Style>
    <!-- The cell gutter (spec.md item 1) as Padding. Theme/Table.axaml applies it as Margin, and on
         a fixed-Width cell in a StackPanel a Margin widens the slot past its header's, moving every
         cell after it out of line. A control-level style beats the application-level one. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.tc-num, TextBlock.cell.tc-text">
      <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0" />
      <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.CellPadding}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- The four ink overrides, and they have to live here rather than be left to
         Theme/Controls.axaml: a control-level style beats an application-level one whatever the
         selectors say, so TextBlock.cell's secondary ink would win over the app's TextBlock.mono
         and TextBlock.worse. Within this file the later block wins, which is why worse is last:
         an outlier's HFR cell matches the quality rule and the outlier-row rule as well. -->

    <!-- The four quality-group cells (HFR, Ecc, FWHM, Stars) carry the primary ink and every
         other numeric cell the secondary one, which is the inputs' type table. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.q">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorTextPrimary}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- A file name is what the user copies and reads, so it takes the primary ink; the mono
         family itself comes from Theme/Controls.axaml's TextBlock.mono. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.mono">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorTextPrimary}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- A row with a finding lifts its whole line to the primary ink, which is the comp's
         .tbl.fr .row.out .c rule: the row a user is hunting for comes forward by weight of ink,
         not by a fill and not by a colour. Driven by FrameRowViewModel.IsOutlier (review ruling
         (a)). -->
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.outlier TextBlock.cell">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorTextPrimary}" />
    </Style>
    <!-- Spec 12.4's three grading band inks, on a cell of this table. Theme/Controls.axaml carries
         the same three rules for every other surface (the grading tally, and Task 7's preview
         badges), and those are where the band classes are defined; they cannot reach a cell here,
         because a control-level style beats an application-level one whatever the selectors say
         and TextBlock.cell, TextBlock.cell.q and the outlier-row rule above would all win over
         them. This block is that same ink, re-declared in this host so it can win over the three,
         and it binds the same brushes. It sits after the row and role inks and before worse.

         The *Value keys spec 12.4's band table names are Color resources; ColorSuccess,
         ColorWarning and ColorError are the SolidColorBrush resources built from exactly those
         colours, and a Foreground binds a brush (questions.md Q14). -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.band-better">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorSuccess}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.band-watch">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorWarning}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.band-reject">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorError}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- The one "worse" ink, on the offending cell and never on the whole row: no fill, no icon,
         no bold (panel-density.md section 5). Last of the ink blocks on purpose, because within
         one style host the later block wins and an outlier's HFR cell matches all four of the
         rules above, the band included: spec 12.4 keeps both marks and the flag is the one that
         gets the ink, because it is the verdict the outlier filter, the findings' counts and the
         night strip's tall ticks all agree on. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.worse">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorMetricWorst}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- Spec.md item 6's faint dash, redeclared here because the local inks above beat
         Theme/Table.axaml's application-level [Text=-] rule. A missing value is never graded or
         flagged, so its order against worse does not matter. -->
    <Style Selector="TextBlock.cell.tc-num[Text=-], TextBlock.cell.tc-text[Text=-]">
      <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ColorTextTertiary}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- The row's base fill and its hover fill (spec 14.5) are both setters. The base one used
         to be a local Background attribute on the Border, and a local value outranks a style
         trigger in Avalonia's value precedence, so the hover fill never rendered at all (review
         finding 2). Anything transparent-by-default in a template that also has a :pointerover
         rule has to be declared this way round. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row:pointerover">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ColorBgHover}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- R9: the night strip's hover, rendered as the row's own hover fill. Not a new token and
         not an accent: spec 14.5 spends light on state and colour on data, and the strip's tick
         is already the data. After the pointerover rule on purpose, because within one style host
         the later block wins and a hovered row may also be the highlighted one. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.highlighted">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ColorBgHover}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- R23's grade tint, after the hover and highlight rules so a tinted row keeps its colour
         under the pointer rather than falling back to the neutral hover. Selection wins: a
         selected tinted row drops its fill so the container's lit field shows. -->
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.tint-watch">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FrameTintWatch}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.tint-reject">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FrameTintReject}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.tint-watch:pointerover, Border.frame-row.tint-watch.highlighted">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FrameTintWatchHover}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="Border.frame-row.tint-reject:pointerover, Border.frame-row.tint-reject.highlighted">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource FrameTintRejectHover}" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox#FrameRows ListBoxItem:selected Border.frame-row.tint-watch, ListBox#FrameRows ListBoxItem:selected Border.frame-row.tint-reject">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
    </Style>
    <Style Selector="ListBox#FrameRows ListBoxItem:selected Border.frame-row:pointerover">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ColorBgHover}" />
    </Style>

    <!-- The item container, the comp's lit row. Its padding, zero minimum and zebra fill are
         Theme/Table.axaml's ListBox.table rules (spec.md item 7); a local Background setter here
         would beat the zebra. Selection is light, not colour (P12 direction): a lighter field plus
         the 2 px lit edge the row template draws. This rule repeats the spine's selected field
         without its accent ink: the frame cells set their ink by local style, and no accent hue
         carries state anywhere on this page, so the metric inks and the filter inks are never read
         as a selection. -->
    <Style Selector="ListBox#FrameRows ListBoxItem:selected /template/ ContentPresenter">
      <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ColorBgElevated}" />
    </Style>
  </UserControl.Styles>

  <!-- Ruling Q11: the frame table answers Ctrl+C and Escape, and nothing else. Ctrl+D, F2 and
       Alt+Left belong to the page shell above it, and Ctrl+A is the ListBox's own.

       Both commands carry a CanExecute, and that is what decides whether the table owns the key
       or lets it go: a KeyBinding whose command reports it cannot execute leaves the event
       unhandled, so an Escape with no filter and no selection bubbles to TargetDetailView's own
       handler and closes the drawer or navigates back (review P2-1, ruling (b)). -->
  <UserControl.KeyBindings>
    <KeyBinding Gesture="Ctrl+C" Command="{Binding CopySelectedPathsCommand}" />
    <KeyBinding Gesture="Escape" Command="{Binding ClearFilterOrSelectionCommand}" />
  </UserControl.KeyBindings>

  <Grid RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,*">
    <!-- The toolbar: the section label, the comp's count line, and the three actions. Outside the
         horizontal ScrollViewer on purpose, so it does not pan away with the columns. -->
    <Grid Grid.Row="0"
          x:Name="FrameTableToolbar"
          ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto,Auto"
          ColumnSpacing="12"
          MinHeight="30"
          Margin="0,0,0,6">
      <!-- The slot's content goes to a second line when the first cannot hold it. -->
      <WrapPanel Grid.Column="0"
                 Orientation="Horizontal"
                 ItemSpacing="12"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center">
        <TextBlock Classes="section"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="Frames" />
        <TextBlock x:Name="ShownCount"
                   Classes="t-caption num"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="{Binding ShownCountText}" />
        <ContentControl x:Name="ToolbarSlot"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      </WrapPanel>
      <Button Grid.Column="1"
              x:Name="CopySelectedPathsButton"
              Classes="sm"
              Content="{Binding CopySelectedPathsText}"
              Command="{Binding CopySelectedPathsCommand}" />
      <Button Grid.Column="2"
              x:Name="RevealSelectedButton"
              Classes="sm"
              Content="Reveal"
              Command="{Binding RevealSelectedCommand}" />

      <!-- The column picker. Each checkbox raises ToggleColumn rather than writing IsVisible
           itself, so the persisted list and the checkboxes cannot disagree. A column whose
           metric group is off is disabled rather than absent: turning it on would change
           nothing visible, and the hint says where the group goes back on. -->
      <Button Grid.Column="3" x:Name="FrameColumnPicker" Classes="sm" Content="Columns">
        <Button.Flyout>
          <Flyout>
            <StackPanel MaxHeight="520">
              <TextBlock Text="A greyed column belongs to a metric group turned off in Settings."
                         MaxWidth="280"
                         TextWrapping="Wrap"
                         Margin="0,0,0,6"
                         Foreground="{DynamicResource ColorTextTertiary}" />
              <ScrollViewer>
                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Columns}">
                  <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate DataType="dash:ColumnViewModel">
                      <CheckBox Content="{Binding Title}"
                                IsChecked="{Binding IsVisible, Mode=OneWay}"
                                IsEnabled="{Binding IsGroupEnabled}"
                                Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).ToggleColumnCommand}"
                                CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                    </DataTemplate>
                  </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                </ItemsControl>
              </ScrollViewer>
            </StackPanel>
          </Flyout>
        </Button.Flyout>
      </Button>
    </Grid>

    <!-- Spec 12.4's legend, the two marked bands only (P24 R23), under the toolbar line and above
         the column header, with the rows it explains. The sentence is not optional chrome: this
         application writes no user file (spec 2.1) and a page that colours frames red owes the
         reader that statement where the colour is. -->
    <WrapPanel Grid.Row="1" x:Name="GradingLegend" Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
      <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" Fill="{DynamicResource ColorWarning}" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,4,0" />
      <TextBlock Classes="t-label muted" Text="watch" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,14,0" />
      <Ellipse Width="8" Height="8" Fill="{DynamicResource ColorError}" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,4,0" />
      <TextBlock Classes="t-label muted" Text="reject" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,14,0" />
      <TextBlock Classes="t-label muted"
                 x:Name="GradingAdvisory"
                 Text="Grading is advisory. No frame is deleted or hidden."
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" />
    </WrapPanel>

    <Grid Grid.Row="2" RowDefinitions="Auto,*">
      <!-- Spec.md item 7's one rule, under the header row, in the brush TableRow draws its header
           edge with; the rows themselves carry no rule. -->
      <Border Grid.Row="0" BorderThickness="0,0,0,1" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource ColorBorderEmphasis}">
      <!-- The header band stops short of the rows' always-drawn vertical bar, so its viewport is
           the rows' viewport: otherwise at the far right the header's offset clamps one bar width
           short of the rows' and every header sits out of line. -->
      <ScrollViewer x:Name="FrameHeaderScroller"
                    Margin="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.ScrollInset}"
                    HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Hidden" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
      <!-- Header row. One cell per column, in FrameColumns.All's order, which is what the
           view-model builds Columns in. -->
      <StackPanel x:Name="FrameTableHeader" Orientation="Horizontal"
                  MinHeight="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.RowMinHeight}">
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[0].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[0].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[0]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />

        <!-- Spec 12.4's Rig column (PAR-004), placed after Time and drawn only on a multi-rig
             night. It is not a FrameColumns entry and it adds no display.columns.frames key
             (task1-report departure 1): it is never hideable and never in the picker, because
             offering a control that does nothing on the single-rig nights that are most of a
             library teaches the wrong model of why a column is missing.

             A plain header rather than the sortable FrameHeaderCell template, whose command keys
             on a column key this column does not have. It takes the existing text column width
             rather than declaring a figure of its own.

             The gutter is Padding and never Margin (review P2-2). Every other header cell is a
             ContentControl of exactly its column's width whose inset lives inside the template,
             so a horizontal Margin here would make this cell wider than the row cell's 90 and
             shift every header after Rig out of its own column. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="RigColumnHeader"
                   Classes="t-label"
                   Width="{StaticResource FrameColTextWidth}"
                   Padding="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.CellPadding}"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="Rig"
                   IsVisible="{Binding IsMultiRig}" />

        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[1].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[1].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[1]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[2].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[2].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[2]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[3].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[3].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[3]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[4].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[4].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[4]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[5].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[5].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[5]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[6].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[6].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[6]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[7].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[7].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[7]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[8].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[8].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[8]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[9].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[9].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[9]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[10].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[10].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[10]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[11].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[11].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[11]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[12].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[12].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[12]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[13].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[13].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[13]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[14].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[14].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[14]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[15].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[15].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[15]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[16].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[16].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[16]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[17].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[17].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[17]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[18].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[18].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[18]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[19].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[19].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[19]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[20].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[20].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[20]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[21].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[21].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[21]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[22].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[22].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[22]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[23].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[23].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[23]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[24].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[24].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[24]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[25].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[25].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[25]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[26].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[26].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[26]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[27].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[27].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[27]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[28].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[28].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[28]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[29].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[29].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[29]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[30].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[30].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[30]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
        <ContentControl Width="{Binding Columns[31].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[31].IsShown}"
                        Content="{Binding Columns[31]}"
                        ContentTemplate="{StaticResource FrameHeaderCell}" />
      </StackPanel>
      </ScrollViewer>
      </Border>

      <!-- FIXER LIST F12. The rows are virtualised, so a 200 frame session realises the two dozen
           rows in the viewport rather than 200 rows of 32 cells each. The VirtualizingStackPanel
           is a ListBox's default and is declared anyway, because it is what keeps that case green.

           A ListBox rather than the ItemsControl this was: spec 12.4's multi-row copy needs a
           selection model, and SelectionMode="Multiple" brings click, Ctrl-click, Shift-click,
           Ctrl+A, and keyboard navigation that would otherwise all be hand-built. SelectedItems is
           not a styled property and cannot be bound in XAML, so FrameTableView.axaml.cs hands the
           view-model's SelectedRows to it once, and from then on the control and the view-model
           share one collection.

           The rows scroll horizontally in the ListBox itself, so its vertical bar sits at the
           viewport's right edge and is always drawn (spec.md item 8, t:Table.Scroller), which
           keeps its reserved width constant; FrameTableView.axaml.cs keeps the header band's
           offset equal to the rows' offset. Classes="table" is the spine's zebra. -->
      <ListBox Grid.Row="1"
               x:Name="FrameRows"
               Classes="table"
               t:Table.Scroller="True"
               ItemsSource="{Binding Rows}"
               SelectionMode="Multiple"
               Background="Transparent"
               BorderThickness="0"
               Padding="0"
               ScrollViewer.VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Visible"
               ScrollViewer.HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
        <ListBox.ItemsPanel>
          <ItemsPanelTemplate>
            <VirtualizingStackPanel />
          </ItemsPanelTemplate>
        </ListBox.ItemsPanel>
        <ListBox.ItemTemplate>
          <DataTemplate DataType="detail:FrameRowViewModel">
            <StackPanel>
              <!-- The 2 px lit edge of the comp's selected row, drawn over the row rather than
                   inside its layout (ruling R16): it lands inside the Time cell's 8 px left
                   gutter, so it needs no layout reserve and a selection moves no cell. -->
              <Grid>
              <Border Classes="frame-row"
                      Classes.outlier="{Binding IsOutlier}"
                      Classes.highlighted="{Binding IsHighlighted}"
                      Classes.tint-watch="{Binding IsScoreWatch}"
                      Classes.tint-reject="{Binding IsScoreReject}"
                      PointerPressed="OnRowPointerPressed"
                      PointerReleased="OnRowPointerReleased"
                      MinHeight="28">
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-text"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[0].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[0].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding TimeText}"
                             Text="{Binding TimeText}" />
                  <!-- The Rig cell, drawn only on a multi-rig night. Its visibility comes from the
                       table rather than from the row, because the rig list is the night's, and it
                       is reached through the same #Root the row's five commands use. -->
                  <TextBlock x:Name="RigCell"
                             Classes="cell tc-text"
                             Width="{StaticResource FrameColTextWidth}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).IsMultiRig}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding RigText}"
                             Text="{Binding RigText}" />
                  <!-- The file name is the cell a user reads and copies, so it is the one text
                       cell in the mono family and in the primary ink.

                       R6: it never trims, and the full path is on the tip (ruling Q8).
                       TextTrimming is set inline rather than by a narrower style selector,
                       because a local value outranks TextBlock.cell.tc-text's setter and that is exactly
                       what is wanted for this one cell. -->
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell mono tc-text"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[1].Width}"
                             TextTrimming="None"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding FilePath}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[1].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding FileName}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-text"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[2].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[2].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding FilterText}"
                             Text="{Binding FilterText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[3].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[3].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding ExposureText}" />
                  <!-- The four quality-group cells take the primary ink (the q class), and the
                       two with a finding take the worse ink on the offending cell alone.

                       Spec 12.4's grading bands are the second mark on the same cells: the flag
                       answers "this night's rules flagged this frame" and the band answers "how
                       far from the baseline this value sits". Both stay. Where a cell carries
                       both, the flag's worse ink wins, because it is the verdict the outlier
                       filter, the findings' counts and the night strip's tall ticks all agree on.
                       What makes it win is this view's own style host, where TextBlock.cell.worse
                       is declared after TextBlock.cell.band-better, .band-watch and .band-reject:
                       within one host the later block wins at equal specificity. It is not
                       Theme/Controls.axaml, whose order is the opposite on purpose (the band wins
                       on the preview badges, which have no control-level host of their own), so an
                       editor who reordered that file to change this cell would change the badges
                       instead and leave this cell where it was. -->
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num q"
                             Classes.band-better="{Binding HfrCell.IsBetter}"
                             Classes.band-watch="{Binding HfrCell.IsWatch}"
                             Classes.band-reject="{Binding HfrCell.IsReject}"
                             Classes.worse="{Binding IsHfrOutlier}"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[4].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[4].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding HfrCell.Tooltip}"
                             Text="{Binding HfrCell.Text}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num q"
                             Classes.band-better="{Binding EccentricityCell.IsBetter}"
                             Classes.band-watch="{Binding EccentricityCell.IsWatch}"
                             Classes.band-reject="{Binding EccentricityCell.IsReject}"
                             Classes.worse="{Binding IsEccentricityOutlier}"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[5].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[5].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding EccentricityCell.Tooltip}"
                             Text="{Binding EccentricityCell.Text}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num q"
                             Classes.band-better="{Binding FwhmCell.IsBetter}"
                             Classes.band-watch="{Binding FwhmCell.IsWatch}"
                             Classes.band-reject="{Binding FwhmCell.IsReject}"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[6].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[6].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding FwhmCell.Tooltip}"
                             Text="{Binding FwhmCell.Text}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num q"
                             Classes.band-better="{Binding DetectedStarsCell.IsBetter}"
                             Classes.band-watch="{Binding DetectedStarsCell.IsWatch}"
                             Classes.band-reject="{Binding DetectedStarsCell.IsReject}"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[7].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[7].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding DetectedStarsCell.Tooltip}"
                             Text="{Binding DetectedStarsCell.Text}" />
                  <!-- Spec 12.4 (Phase 15A): the guiding RMS cell carries a dagger only when
                       guiding_rms_source is phd2, never for csv, because the CSV sidecar is the
                       frame's own file and needs no disclosure. The dagger is decorative to a
                       screen reader (AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw", the codebase's
                       only user of that property so far); the value cell's AutomationProperties.Name
                       carries the figure and the source sentence together (review P2-3: the name
                       must not replace the figure), and is the figure alone when the source is not
                       phd2. -->
                  <Grid Width="{Binding Columns[8].Width}"
                        IsVisible="{Binding Columns[8].IsShown}">
                    <!-- The RMS cell keeps its source mark and its provenance tooltip beside it,
                         and gains a band and a deviation tooltip of its own. The spec grades this
                         column against the night's own baseline; the web application does not
                         grade it at all (questions.md Q7). The value fills the cell with the
                         gutter padding every number has, so its digits end at Width - Gutter on
                         every row, which is where the header title ends. The mark is a
                         gutter-wide box over the right gutter, flush after the digits with no
                         space; a dagger wider than the box (the label tier at a large root size)
                         draws on into the next column's left gutter, never onto its text. -->
                    <TextBlock x:Name="GuidingRmsValueCell"
                               Classes="cell tc-num"
                               Classes.band-better="{Binding GuidingRmsCell.IsBetter}"
                               Classes.band-watch="{Binding GuidingRmsCell.IsWatch}"
                               Classes.band-reject="{Binding GuidingRmsCell.IsReject}"
                               ToolTip.Tip="{Binding GuidingRmsCell.Tooltip}"
                               AutomationProperties.Name="{Binding GuidingRmsAccessibleName}"
                               Text="{Binding GuidingRmsCell.Text}" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="GuidingRmsMarkCell"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                               Width="{x:Static t:TableMetrics.Gutter}"
                               Classes="cell t-label"
                               Text="{Binding GuidingRmsSourceGlyph}"
                               IsVisible="{Binding HasGuidingRmsSource}"
                               ToolTip.Tip="{Binding GuidingRmsSourceTooltip}"
                               AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
                  </Grid>
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[9].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[9].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding GuidingRmsRaText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[10].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[10].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding GuidingRmsDecText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[11].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[11].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AduMeanText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Classes.band-better="{Binding AduMedianCell.IsBetter}"
                             Classes.band-watch="{Binding AduMedianCell.IsWatch}"
                             Classes.band-reject="{Binding AduMedianCell.IsReject}"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[12].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[12].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding AduMedianCell.Tooltip}"
                             Text="{Binding AduMedianCell.Text}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[13].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[13].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AduStdevText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[14].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[14].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AduMinText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[15].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[15].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AduMaxText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[16].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[16].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding FocuserPositionText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[17].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[17].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding FocuserTempText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[18].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[18].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AmbientTempText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[19].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[19].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding DewPointText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[20].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[20].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding HumidityText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[21].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[21].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding PressureText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[22].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[22].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding WindSpeedText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[23].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[23].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding WindDirectionText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[24].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[24].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding WindGustText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[25].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[25].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding CloudCoverText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[26].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[26].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding SkyQualityText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[27].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[27].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding AirmassText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-text"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[28].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[28].IsShown}"
                             ToolTip.Tip="{Binding PierSideText}"
                             Text="{Binding PierSideText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[29].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[29].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding RotatorPositionText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[30].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[30].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding SensorTempText}" />
                  <TextBlock Classes="cell tc-num"
                             Width="{Binding Columns[31].Width}"
                             IsVisible="{Binding Columns[31].IsShown}"
                             Text="{Binding CameraGainText}" />

                  <!-- Spec 12.4's five per-frame actions, behind one row-end button so the row
                       stays readable. Open preview is spec 11.5's modal and stays disabled until
                       Phase 8 binds the delegate. -->
                  <Button Content="..." Padding="6,0" Margin="8,0,0,0">
                    <Button.Flyout>
                      <Flyout>
                        <StackPanel Spacing="2">
                          <Button Content="Open preview"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                  Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).OpenPreviewCommand}"
                                  CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                          <Button Content="Reveal in Explorer"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                  Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).RevealFrameCommand}"
                                  CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                          <Button Content="Open with default application"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                  Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).OpenFrameWithDefaultApplicationCommand}"
                                  CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                          <Button Content="Copy path"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                  Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).CopyFramePathCommand}"
                                  CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                          <Button Content="Show raw headers"
                                  HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                  HorizontalContentAlignment="Left"
                                  Command="{Binding #Root.((detail:FrameTableViewModel)DataContext).ToggleRawHeadersCommand}"
                                  CommandParameter="{Binding}" />
                        </StackPanel>
                      </Flyout>
                    </Button.Flyout>
                  </Button>
                </StackPanel>
              </Border>
              <Rectangle Width="2"
                         HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                         Fill="{DynamicResource ColorAccent}"
                         IsVisible="{Binding $parent[ListBoxItem].IsSelected}" />
              </Grid>

              <!-- Task 6's raw header panel, behind the row's own flag. RawHeaders is null until
                   ToggleRawHeadersCommand builds it on this row's first expansion, so a session of
                   400 frames never holds 400 header queries; content stays bound to the panel
                   view-model even after the row collapses, so re-expanding does not rebuild it. -->
              <ContentControl x:Name="RawHeaderRegion"
                              Margin="0,4,0,4"
                              IsVisible="{Binding AreRawHeadersExpanded}"
                              Content="{Binding RawHeaders}">
                <ContentControl.ContentTemplate>
                  <DataTemplate DataType="detail:RawHeaderPanelViewModel">
                    <controls:RawHeaderPanel />
                  </DataTemplate>
                </ContentControl.ContentTemplate>
              </ContentControl>
            </StackPanel>
          </DataTemplate>
        </ListBox.ItemTemplate>
      </ListBox>
    </Grid>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>
